Issue #12 item N2 -- mutation evidence for retiring go2rtc's nginx routes
================================================================================

Premise verification (executed before any change)
---------------------------------------------------
Confirmed directly against tests/nginx-parity/vendor/nginx.conf (corvette):
exactly five locations proxy to the `go2rtc` upstream, and no others do:

  $ grep -n "proxy_pass http://go2rtc" tests/nginx-parity/vendor/nginx.conf
  204:            proxy_pass http://go2rtc/api/ws;      (location /live/mse/api/ws)
  213:            proxy_pass http://go2rtc/api/ws;      (location /live/webrtc/api/ws)
  223:            proxy_pass http://go2rtc/webrtc.html; (location /live/webrtc/webrtc.html)
  233:            proxy_pass http://go2rtc/api;          (location /api/go2rtc/api)
  243:            proxy_pass http://go2rtc/api/webrtc;   (location /api/go2rtc/webrtc)

Matches the plan's own Premise count exactly (5, not 2). /live/jsmpeg/
(nginx.conf:192) proxies to the `jsmpeg` upstream, confirmed not `go2rtc` --
out of scope for this item, used below as the "did not touch more than it
claims" regression check.

Setup
-----
docker/scripts/patch_pkg_location.py, then docker/scripts/
patch_live_hls_location.py (N1), then this item's own new docker/scripts/
patch_retire_go2rtc_routes.py -- all three from frigate-vulkan -- applied in
sequence to a scratch copy of corvette's own tests/nginx-parity/vendor/
nginx.conf, then tests/nginx-parity/offline.patch applied on top for
unprivileged local execution, exactly the chain N1's own evidence log used,
extended by this item's own third script. A real nginx 1.30.4 (from `nix
develop`) serves this config. Three plain nginx stub servers stand in for
the upstreams this file's proxied locations need: a combined Frigate/mqtt/
jsmpeg stub on 127.0.0.1:15001 (offline.patch's own fixed stub port -- also
answers /auth 202 for every auth_request subrequest), and a stand-in for
G2's own fMP4-over-WebSocket listener on 127.0.0.1:8555 (the exact port
this item's own new `corvette_fmp4_ws` upstream names, matching N1's
`corvette_hls`/8556 precedent -- not a free port choice). No go2rtc stub
is started at all: proving these five routes no longer reach go2rtc means
proving nothing is listening where they used to point and the app still
answers correctly regardless.

scripts/route_parity.sh (issue #12 INV-4) is the assertion harness, run
against a 7-row local table (n2-route-rows.table): /live/jsmpeg/ (regression),
the five named go2rtc-proxied locations, and the new /live/mse/ws/ replacement.
A dedicated, separate static assertion (`grep -c "proxy_pass http://go2rtc"`
on the served nginx.conf, expect 0) is the "ALL FIVE are gone" check the
plan's own Mutation text asks for, distinct from the per-route table rows.

Patch chain command (both runs use the same three-script + offline.patch
chain; only the presence of one location block differs between them):

  python3 patch_pkg_location.py nginx.conf
  python3 patch_live_hls_location.py nginx.conf
  python3 patch_retire_go2rtc_routes.py nginx.conf
  patch -p1 -F0 -d conf -i offline.patch

Real output (fresh chain, from the pristine vendored donor):

  patch_pkg_location: /pkg/ location inserted
  patch_live_hls_location: /live/hls/ location inserted
  patch_retire_go2rtc_routes: five go2rtc-proxied locations removed, /live/mse/ws/ inserted
  patching file nginx.conf
  Hunk #5 succeeded at 72 (offset 10 lines).
  Hunk #6 succeeded at 82 (offset 10 lines).
  Hunk #7 succeeded at 89 (offset 10 lines).
  Hunk #8 succeeded at 118 (offset 10 lines).
  Hunk #9 succeeded at 134 (offset 10 lines).
  Hunk #10 succeeded at 145 (offset 10 lines).
  patching file go2rtc_upstream.conf
  patching file auth_location.conf

(The six offset-only reports are expected and benign: patch's own -F0 forbids
fuzzy context matching, so every hunk above still had to find its context
text byte-for-byte -- the reported "offset" is only a line-number shift
caused by patch_pkg_location.py's and patch_live_hls_location.py's own
earlier insertions landing before offline.patch's hunks, not a sign any hunk
landed somewhere unintended. None of offline.patch's hunks touch the /live/*
or /api/go2rtc/* location group or the corvette_hls/corvette_fmp4_ws
upstream declarations this item's own script edits, confirmed by inspection
of offline.patch itself.)

--- BROKEN (four of the five removed correctly, /api/go2rtc/webrtc left in place) -- FAIL ---

Real diff applied to the correctly-patched nginx.conf (the only edit made for
this run):

  198,208d197
  <         # MUTATION: simulates N2 forgetting to remove this one route while
  <         # the other four were removed correctly.
  <         location /api/go2rtc/webrtc {
  <             include auth_request.conf;
  <             limit_except POST {
  <                 deny  all;
  <             }
  <             proxy_pass http://go2rtc/api/webrtc;
  <             include proxy.conf;
  <         }
  <

Command:
  bash scripts/route_parity.sh --table n2-route-rows.table --mode local \
    --base-url http://127.0.0.1:18995

  ok   /live/jsmpeg/: 200 application/octet-stream
  ok   /live/mse/api/ws: 200 text/html
  ok   /live/webrtc/api/ws: 200 text/html
  ok   /live/webrtc/webrtc.html: 200 text/html
  ok   /api/go2rtc/api: 200 application/octet-stream
  FAIL /api/go2rtc/webrtc: status 403, expected 200
  ok   /live/mse/ws/front_door: 200 application/octet-stream
  route_parity: 7/7 rows checked, 1 failed

Dedicated "ALL FIVE are gone" static assertion:

  $ grep -c "proxy_pass http://go2rtc" nginx.conf
  1
  ASSERTION: FAIL -- not all five go2rtc routes are gone

Confirms the defect exactly as the plan's Mutation text describes:
/live/jsmpeg/ stayed unaffected throughout (proving this item did not touch
more than it claims); the four routes that WERE actually removed in this
broken state show correctly-removed behaviour (their own rows pass, showing
they were removed); the one left in place is caught twice over -- its own
route_parity row fails (403, not the expected fallen-through content,
because a plain GET now hits the surviving location's own `limit_except
POST` guard instead of proxying anywhere), and the dedicated combined
assertion independently fails (count=1, not 0). Neither check alone would
be redundant with the other: the row-level check catches this specific
route because it happens to respond differently; the dedicated grep check
is what the plan asks for as the assertion that names the true invariant
("all five, unconditionally") regardless of how an individual leftover
route happens to answer a probe.

