Confirms the fix: restoring the exact removed block returns all seven rows
to passing and the dedicated combined assertion to zero, matching the
BROKEN run above with only the one block's presence differing.

Route-behaviour finding (Do step 4, established, not assumed)
---------------------------------------------------------------
The five removed routes do NOT all fail the same way, confirmed by the
PASS run above:
  - the three /live/* ones (/live/mse/api/ws, /live/webrtc/api/ws,
    /live/webrtc/webrtc.html) have no other /live/* location to catch them,
    so they fall all the way through to the site's own SPA shell: 200,
    text/html, containing id="root" and an /assets/main- reference -- the
    same "unmatched path" failure mode tests/route-parity/expectations'
    existing /go2rtc/stream.html row already documents.
  - the two /api/go2rtc/* ones (/api/go2rtc/api, /api/go2rtc/webrtc) DO
    match the broader, pre-existing `location /api/` prefix once their own
    more specific location is gone, so they proxy through to Frigate's own
    API instead of the SPA shell -- confirmed reaching the harness's stub
    (not the SPA shell, not a connection failure); their real Frigate-
    backend answer is deliberately left untabled in
    tests/route-parity/expectations, since a stub is not a source for what
    Frigate's own API actually answers for a path it never defined.

